>> title: Lahm bi Ajeen
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: lamb, bread, yeast, oven, pomegranate molasses, lebanese
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: lahm bi ajeen, lahm b'ajine, lahm bajin, lahmajun, lahmacun, sfiha, sfeeha, sfeeha baalbakia, meat pie, Arabic meat flatbread
>> pairs-with: pomegranate-molasses, sumac-onions, labneh
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 45 min
>> step.1: knead 8 min, prove 1 1/2 hr
>> step.2: drain the tomato and onion 20 min
>> step.3: work the meat through the paste
>> step.4: roll thin, spread to the very edge
>> step.5: bake at 500°F 8 min

Knead @all-purpose flour{3%cups}(390 g), @instant yeast{1 1/2%tsp}(5 g), @fine sea salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g), @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @warm water{1%cup}(240 mL) ~knead{8%min} to a firm, smooth dough, then ~prove{1 1/2%hr} covered until doubled.

Salt @ripe tomatoes{2}(250 g; grated, skins discarded) and @yellow onion{1%medium}(grated) with @kosher salt{1%tsp} and ~drain{20%min} in a sieve, pressing at the end.

Work @ground lamb{12%oz}(340 g; fatty shoulder), @pomegranate molasses{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @tomato paste{1%Tbs}(15 g), @ground allspice{1%tsp}, @Aleppo pepper{1%tsp}, @ground cinnamon{1/4%tsp} and @pine nuts{2%Tbs} into @&(~1)drained tomato and onion{} until it is a spreadable paste rather than a mince.

Roll @&(~3)proved dough{} into eight rounds barely thicker than paper and spread @&(~1)meat paste{} over each one right to the rim in a thin, even film.

Bake @&(~1)topped rounds{} on a hot #baking steel{} in the #oven{} at 500°F (260°C) ~bake{8%min}, until the edges blister and the meat has just lost its raw colour.
